<!--
  Simulation definition of the Pantsir-S1 point-defence launcher.

  Deliberately inert as far as KSA is concerned: mass, colliders and an attach node, nothing
  more. All the behaviour lives in the C# mod, which looks for a part with this Id on the
  vehicle and mounts the battery there. That split avoids having to register a custom module
  type into the engine's internal update lists, which is not reachable without patching.

  Collider boxes are axis-aligned in part space: X up, Y along the vehicle, Z across it. The
  hull box starts at X = 0 so the vehicle rests on its wheels rather than sinking to its
  chassis rails.
-->
<Assets>

  <!--
    Its own category in the part picker, rather than filed under Structural where a Phalanx mount
    sits next to girders. EditorTag is a string rather than an enum and the picker draws a row per
    registered tag, so this is a supported extension: Core's own CoreEditorTagsGameData.xml says
    so in a comment addressed to modders.

    The three flags are copied from Structural and are not decoration. Structural carries
    RootPartWhitelist, FaceSnapTargetWhitelist and DiameterFilterlist, and moving a part off it
    without them silently drops the launcher's ability to be a craft's root part, stops anything
    face-snapping to it, and removes it from diameter filtering. None of that fails loudly.

    Named for the job rather than for this mod on purpose. The lookup is keyed on the string, so a
    second weapons mod declaring "Weapons" shares this tab instead of adding a near-duplicate.
    There is no way to filter within a tab by mod or manufacturer; docs/BLOCKED-ON-KSA.md has why.
  -->
  <EditorTagDef Id="Weapons" RootPartWhitelist="true" FaceSnapTargetWhitelist="true"
                DiameterFilterlist="true" />

  <!--
    Beside it rather than inside it, because a camera is not a weapon. It shoots at nothing, it is
    useful on a craft that carries no armament at all, and filing it under Weapons would say the
    opposite of what it is.

    Same three flags, but RootPartWhitelist does nothing for the director as it stands: the
    editor rejects any part carrying a ToSurface connector whatever its tags say, and a head that
    bolts to anything needs one. It is here for a sensor that stacks instead. An observation post
    is a hull with a director on it, so the hull is the root and this is the passenger.
  -->
  <EditorTagDef Id="Sensors" RootPartWhitelist="true" FaceSnapTargetWhitelist="true"
                DiameterFilterlist="true" />

  <PartGameData Id="KSArmory_Prefab_Launcher6" DisplayName="Pantsir-S1 Point Defence System">
    <EditorTag Value="Weapons" />

    <!--
      Not Radial, unlike the stores below. That tag is on the editor's face-snap target
      *blacklist*, and the blacklist beats the Weapons whitelist, so while it was here nothing
      could be mounted on the launcher, an EO director included. A vehicle is something you bolt
      things to.
    -->
    <EditorTag Value="NoFaceSnapping" />
    <Diameter M="3" />

    <!--
      A node connector, at the part origin, which is the underside. No ToSurface, and that is
      what lets the launcher start a craft: VehicleEditor.IsAllowedAsRootPart rejects a part if
      *any* of its connectors is ToSurface or FromSurface, whatever tags it carries. So a vehicle
      root and a radially-attached part are mutually exclusive in KSA, and this is a truck.

      NoFaceSnapping above is the other half. Face snapping is a separate route onto a surface
      that a ToSurface connector suppresses, so dropping the flag would otherwise switch this
      part onto it, and it aligns the part's -Z to the surface where the connector path aligns
      the connector's -X. +X is up on this hull, so that lays an 8x8 truck on its side.
    -->
    <Connector Id="_adConnectorAft" />

    <!--
      Makes the launcher a command source in its own right, so a craft that is only this has
      something to control it. Without it KSA will not fly one.
    -->
    <Control />

    <!-- Onboard cell, so the unit is not dead weight when detached from a host craft. -->
    <Battery>
      <MaximumCapacity J="2000" />
    </Battery>

    <!-- Combat weight of a real Pantsir-S1 on its KAMAZ-6560: about thirty tonnes. -->
    <SolidSphereMass>
      <Mass Kg="30000" />
      <Radius M="2.00" />
    </SolidSphereMass>

    <Collider Id="KSArmory_Collider">
      <!-- Chassis and running gear, resting on the ground plane at X = 0. -->
      <Box Id="KSArmory_HullCollider">
        <LocationAsmb X="1.03" Y="0.05" Z="0" />
        <Collider2Asmb X="0" Y="0" Z="0" />
        <LengthX M="2.06" />
        <LengthY M="7.98" />
        <LengthZ M="2.96" />
      </Box>
      <!-- Cab. -->
      <Box Id="KSArmory_CabCollider">
        <LocationAsmb X="2.55" Y="2.77" Z="0" />
        <Collider2Asmb X="0" Y="0" Z="0" />
        <LengthX M="1.00" />
        <LengthY M="2.18" />
        <LengthZ M="2.60" />
      </Box>
      <!-- Turret body. -->
      <Box Id="KSArmory_TurretCollider">
        <LocationAsmb X="2.75" Y="-1.42" Z="0" />
        <Collider2Asmb X="0" Y="0" Z="0" />
        <LengthX M="1.40" />
        <LengthY M="3.20" />
        <LengthZ M="2.50" />
      </Box>
      <!-- Elevated missile pods and the search radar above them. -->
      <Box Id="KSArmory_PodCollider">
        <LocationAsmb X="4.30" Y="-0.90" Z="0" />
        <Collider2Asmb X="0" Y="0" Z="0" />
        <LengthX M="2.70" />
        <LengthY M="2.60" />
        <LengthZ M="2.90" />
      </Box>
    </Collider>
  </PartGameData>

